[[1,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Undo the fixing nut (1a) and remove the moving tensioner (1b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/223001643.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Fit the moving tensioner and tighten the fixing bolt to torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>dia</p></th><th><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>MOBILE TIMING TENSIONER</p></td><td><p>M8 X 1.25</p></td><td><p>2.8</p></td></tr></table></div>"],[4,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Undo the nut (1a) and remove the mobile timing belt tensioner (1b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/223001644.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[4,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Position the moving timing system tensioner in its housing and secure it without tightening the nut.</p>"],[8,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Undo the bolts (1a) and remove the mobile timing belt tensioner (1b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/223001645.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[8,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Use a suitable tool (e.g. vice) to set the chain tensioner and hold it fully back with a retaining pin.</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>If a new mobile timing belt tensioner is fitted, this is supplied by Part already set and held fully back with a pin.</p></aside><p>1. Position the fixed timing tensioner (1a) in its housing and secure it tightening the bolt (1b) to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>dia</p></th><th><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>MOBILE TIMING TENSIONER</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td><p>(Cylinder head side) 0.8 - 1.0</p></td></tr></table></div><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Once the timing chain has been fitted, remove the mobile tensioner pin and check that the mobile tensioner piston is in contact with the pad.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/223001646.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[32,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Undo the nut.</p><p>2. Remove the timing belt moving tensioner.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/223001647.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[32,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Fit the timing belt moving tensioner.</p><p>Screw in the fixing nut without tightening it.</p>"],[16,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Undo the bolt (1a) loosened previously completely and remove the mobile timing belt tensioner (1b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/223001648.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[16,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Position the moving timing system tensioner in its housing and secure it without tightening the nut.</p>"],[2,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Undo the nut (1a) loosened previously and remove the mobile tensioner (1b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/199001571.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>- Position the moving tensioner in its housing and secure it without tightening the nut.</p>"]]